+# The widest of `charged_pion_integrand`'s three support edges, in the pion
+# rest frame, and therefore the single bound that clips none of them:
+#
+#   pi -> mu nu gamma           (MPI^2 - MMU^2) / (2 MPI) = 29.792142
+#   the boosted muon spectrum   ENG_GAM_MAX_PIRG          = 69.783458
+#   pi -> e nu gamma            (MPI^2 - ME^2)  / (2 MPI) = 69.784260
+#
+# Derived from this file's own MPI and ME rather than typed, and 8.0e-4
+# MeV above ENG_GAM_MAX_PIRG -- close enough that the follow-up quotes
+# both as "69.783", far enough that using the legacy literal as the bound
+# would truncate the electron channel's last sliver. A bound wider than
+# the support only admits zeros; a narrower one silently drops physics.
+cdef double ENG_GAM_MAX_PIRF = (MPI * MPI - ME * ME) / (2.0 * MPI)
+
 
